// F12: check the *published* declaration file itself. The main program
// (tsconfig.json) includes types/index.d.ts but sets `skipLibCheck: true`, so
// tsc never reports a semantic error inside it before the package ships.
//
// Deliberately narrow, so the gate reports defects in our own declarations
// rather than third-party library noise:
//   * `include` is the single published declaration. The domain modules its
//     `TowerConfig` alias names are type-resolved with it, so a broken
//     reference there is caught too.
//   * `types: ["node"]` supplies the Node globals those referenced modules use
//     (`Buffer`, ...). With `skipLibCheck: false` @types/node is checked as a
//     library and must stay clean; `types: []` would instead fail on `Buffer`,
//     which is not a declaration error.
//   * `checkJs: false` keeps this gate about declarations: referenced JS is
//     resolved for its types, not re-linted (tsconfig.json checks JS bodies).
//   * `lib: ["ES2022"]` drops the DOM lib the base config picks up implicitly,
//     so the declaration cannot quietly depend on browser globals.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "skipLibCheck": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "types": [
      "node"
    ],
    "lib": [
      "ES2022"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "types/index.d.ts"
  ]
}
